      "message": "We hit the same crash on real AST2600 hardware (static layout, ACTIVE_BMC_MAX_ALLOWED\u003d1), and it does not need a second update there: with one active BMC allowed, the running version holds the only Update object, so freeSpace() erases it on the very first update. The daemon aborted a few seconds after each of five stagings, and the staged image was no longer listed after the restart.\n\nI had posted https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/+/97245 before finding this one and will abandon mine in favor of this change.",
